{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source; cat -n fsm.go future.go'","aggregated_output":"     1\t// Copyright IBM Corp. 2013, 2025\n     2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n     3\t\n     4\tpackage raft\n     5\t\n     6\timport (\n     7\t\t\"fmt\"\n     8\t\t\"io\"\n     9\t\t\"time\"\n    10\t\n    11\t\thclog \"github.com/hashicorp/go-hclog\"\n    12\t\t\"github.com/hashicorp/go-metrics\"\n    13\t)\n    14\t\n    15\t// FSM is implemented by clients to make use of the replicated log.\n    16\ttype FSM interface {\n    17\t\t// Apply is called once a log entry is committed by a majority of the cluster.\n    18\t\t//\n    19\t\t// Apply should apply the log to the FSM. Apply must be deterministic and\n    20\t\t// produce the same result on all peers in the cluster.\n    21\t\t//\n    22\t\t// The returned value is returned to the client as the ApplyFuture.Response.\n    23\t\tApply(*Log) interface{}\n    24\t\n    25\t\t// Snapshot returns an FSMSnapshot used to: support log compaction, to\n    26\t\t// restore the FSM to a previous state, or to bring out-of-date followers up\n    27\t\t// to a recent log index.\n    28\t\t//\n    29\t\t// The Snapshot implementation should return quickly, because Apply can not\n    30\t\t// be called while Snapshot is running. Generally this means Snapshot should\n    31\t\t// only capture a pointer to the state, and any expensive IO should happen\n    32\t\t// as part of FSMSnapshot.Persist.\n    33\t\t//\n    34\t\t// Apply and Snapshot are always called from the same thread, but Apply will\n    35\t\t// be called concurrently with FSMSnapshot.Persist. This means the FSM should\n    36\t\t// be implemented to allow for concurrent updates while a snapshot is happening.\n    37\t\t//\n    38\t\t// Clients of this library should make no assumptions about whether a returned\n    39\t\t// Snapshot() will actually be stored by Raft. In fact it's quite possible that\n    40\t\t// any Snapshot returned by this call will be discarded, and that\n    41\t\t// FSMSnapshot.Persist will never be called. Raft will always call\n    42\t\t// FSMSnapshot.Release however.\n    43\t\tSnapshot() (FSMSnapshot, error)\n    44\t\n    45\t\t// Restore is used to restore an FSM from a snapshot. It is not called\n    46\t\t// concurrently with any other command. The FSM must discard all previous\n    47\t\t// state before restoring the snapshot.\n    48\t\tRestore(snapshot io.ReadCloser) error\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\t// BatchingFSM extends the FSM interface to add an ApplyBatch function. This can\n    52\t// optionally be implemented by clients to enable multiple logs to be applied to\n    53\t// the FSM in batches. Up to MaxAppendEntries could be sent in a batch.\n    54\ttype BatchingFSM interface {\n    55\t\t// ApplyBatch is invoked once a batch of log entries has been committed and\n    56\t\t// are ready to be applied to the FSM. ApplyBatch will take in an array of\n    57\t\t// log entries. These log entries will be in the order they were committed,\n    58\t\t// will not have gaps, and could be of a few log types. Clients should check\n    59\t\t// the log type prior to attempting to decode the data attached. Presently\n    60\t\t// the LogCommand and LogConfiguration types will be sent.\n    61\t\t//\n    62\t\t// The returned slice must be the same length as the input and each response\n    63\t\t// should correlate to the log at the same index of the input. The returned\n    64\t\t// values will be made available in the ApplyFuture returned by Raft.Apply\n    65\t\t// method if that method was called on the same Raft node as the FSM.\n    66\t\tApplyBatch([]*Log) []interface{}\n    67\t\n    68\t\tFSM\n    69\t}\n    70\t\n    71\t// FSMSnapshot is returned by an FSM in response to a Snapshot\n    72\t// It must be safe to invoke FSMSnapshot methods with concurrent\n    73\t// calls to Apply.\n    74\ttype FSMSnapshot interface {\n    75\t\t// Persist should dump all necessary state to the WriteCloser 'sink',\n    76\t\t// and call sink.Close() when finished or call sink.Cancel() on error.\n    77\t\tPersist(sink SnapshotSink) error\n    78\t\n    79\t\t// Release is invoked when we are finished with the snapshot.\n    80\t\tRelease()\n    81\t}\n    82\t\n    83\t// runFSM is a long running goroutine responsible for applying logs\n    84\t// to the FSM. This is done async of other logs since we don't want\n    85\t// the FSM to block our internal operations.\n    86\tfunc (r *Raft) runFSM() {\n    87\t\tvar lastIndex, lastTerm uint64\n    88\t\n    89\t\tbatchingFSM, batchingEnabled := r.fsm.(BatchingFSM)\n    90\t\tconfigStore, configStoreEnabled := r.fsm.(ConfigurationStore)\n    91\t\n    92\t\tapplySingle := func(req *commitTuple) {\n    93\t\t\t// Apply the log if a command or config change\n    94\t\t\tvar resp interface{}\n    95\t\t\t// Make sure we send a response\n    96\t\t\tdefer func() {\n    97\t\t\t\t// Invoke the future if given\n    98\t\t\t\tif req.future != nil {\n    99\t\t\t\t\treq.future.response = resp\n   100\t\t\t\t\treq.future.respond(nil)\n   101\t\t\t\t}\n   102\t\t\t}()\n   103\t\n   104\t\t\tswitch req.log.Type {\n   105\t\t\tcase LogCommand:\n   106\t\t\t\tstart := time.Now()\n   107\t\t\t\tresp = r.fsm.Apply(req.log)\n   108\t\t\t\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"apply\"}, start)\n   109\t\n   110\t\t\tcase LogConfiguration:\n   111\t\t\t\tif !configStoreEnabled {\n   112\t\t\t\t\t// Return early to avoid incrementing the index and term for\n   113\t\t\t\t\t// an unimplemented operation.\n   114\t\t\t\t\treturn\n   115\t\t\t\t}\n   116\t\n   117\t\t\t\tstart := time.Now()\n   118\t\t\t\tconfigStore.StoreConfiguration(req.log.Index, DecodeConfiguration(req.log.Data))\n   119\t\t\t\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"store_config\"}, start)\n   120\t\t\t}\n   121\t\n   122\t\t\t// Update the indexes\n   123\t\t\tlastIndex = req.log.Index\n   124\t\t\tlastTerm = req.log.Term\n   125\t\t}\n   126\t\n   127\t\tapplyBatch := func(reqs []*commitTuple) {\n   128\t\t\tif !batchingEnabled {\n   129\t\t\t\tfor _, ct := range reqs {\n   130\t\t\t\t\tapplySingle(ct)\n   131\t\t\t\t}\n   132\t\t\t\treturn\n   133\t\t\t}\n   134\t\n   135\t\t\t// Only send LogCommand and LogConfiguration log types. LogBarrier types\n   136\t\t\t// will not be sent to the FSM.\n   137\t\t\tshouldSend := func(l *Log) bool {\n   138\t\t\t\tswitch l.Type {\n   139\t\t\t\tcase LogCommand, LogConfiguration:\n   140\t\t\t\t\treturn true\n   141\t\t\t\t}\n   142\t\t\t\treturn false\n   143\t\t\t}\n   144\t\n   145\t\t\tvar lastBatchIndex, lastBatchTerm uint64\n   146\t\t\tsendLogs := make([]*Log, 0, len(reqs))\n   147\t\t\tfor _, req := range reqs {\n   148\t\t\t\tif shouldSend(req.log) {\n   149\t\t\t\t\tsendLogs = append(sendLogs, req.log)\n   150\t\t\t\t}\n   151\t\t\t\tlastBatchIndex = req.log.Index\n   152\t\t\t\tlastBatchTerm = req.log.Term\n   153\t\t\t}\n   154\t\n   155\t\t\tvar responses []interface{}\n   156\t\t\tif len(sendLogs) > 0 {\n   157\t\t\t\tstart := time.Now()\n   158\t\t\t\tresponses = batchingFSM.ApplyBatch(sendLogs)\n   159\t\t\t\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"applyBatch\"}, start)\n   160\t\t\t\tmetrics.AddSample([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"applyBatchNum\"}, float32(len(reqs)))\n   161\t\n   162\t\t\t\t// Ensure we get the expected responses\n   163\t\t\t\tif len(sendLogs) != len(responses) {\n   164\t\t\t\t\tpanic(\"invalid number of responses\")\n   165\t\t\t\t}\n   166\t\t\t}\n   167\t\n   168\t\t\t// Update the indexes\n   169\t\t\tlastIndex = lastBatchIndex\n   170\t\t\tlastTerm = lastBatchTerm\n   171\t\n   172\t\t\tvar i int\n   173\t\t\tfor _, req := range reqs {\n   174\t\t\t\tvar resp interface{}\n   175\t\t\t\t// If the log was sent to the FSM, retrieve the response.\n   176\t\t\t\tif shouldSend(req.log) {\n   177\t\t\t\t\tresp = responses[i]\n   178\t\t\t\t\ti++\n   179\t\t\t\t}\n   180\t\n   181\t\t\t\tif req.future != nil {\n   182\t\t\t\t\treq.future.response = resp\n   183\t\t\t\t\treq.future.respond(nil)\n   184\t\t\t\t}\n   185\t\t\t}\n   186\t\t}\n   187\t\n   188\t\trestore := func(req *restoreFuture) {\n   189\t\t\t// Open the snapshot\n   190\t\t\tmeta, source, err := r.snapshots.Open(req.ID)\n   191\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   192\t\t\t\treq.respond(fmt.Errorf(\"failed to open snapshot %v: %v\", req.ID, err))\n   193\t\t\t\treturn\n   194\t\t\t}\n   195\t\t\tdefer func() { _ = source.Close() }()\n   196\t\n   197\t\t\tsnapLogger := r.logger.With(\n   198\t\t\t\t\"id\", req.ID,\n   199\t\t\t\t\"last-index\", meta.Index,\n   200\t\t\t\t\"last-term\", meta.Term,\n   201\t\t\t\t\"size-in-bytes\", meta.Size,\n   202\t\t\t)\n   203\t\n   204\t\t\t// Attempt to restore\n   205\t\t\tif err := fsmRestoreAndMeasure(snapLogger, r.fsm, source, meta.Size); err != nil {\n   206\t\t\t\treq.respond(fmt.Errorf(\"failed to restore snapshot %v: %v\", req.ID, err))\n   207\t\t\t\treturn\n   208\t\t\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t\t\t// Update the last index and term\n   211\t\t\tlastIndex = meta.Index\n   212\t\t\tlastTerm = meta.Term\n   213\t\t\treq.respond(nil)\n   214\t\t}\n   215\t\n   216\t\tsnapshot := func(req *reqSnapshotFuture) {\n   217\t\t\t// Is there something to snapshot?\n   218\t\t\tif lastIndex == 0 {\n   219\t\t\t\treq.respond(ErrNothingNewToSnapshot)\n   220\t\t\t\treturn\n   221\t\t\t}\n   222\t\n   223\t\t\t// Start a snapshot\n   224\t\t\tstart := time.Now()\n   225\t\t\tsnap, err := r.fsm.Snapshot()\n   226\t\t\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"snapshot\"}, start)\n   227\t\n   228\t\t\t// Respond to the request\n   229\t\t\treq.index = lastIndex\n   230\t\t\treq.term = lastTerm\n   231\t\t\treq.snapshot = snap\n   232\t\t\treq.respond(err)\n   233\t\t}\n   234\t\n   235\t\tsaturation := newSaturationMetric([]string{\"raft\", \"thread\", \"fsm\", \"saturation\"}, 1*time.Second)\n   236\t\n   237\t\tfor {\n   238\t\t\tsaturation.sleeping()\n   239\t\n   240\t\t\tselect {\n   241\t\t\tcase ptr := <-r.fsmMutateCh:\n   242\t\t\t\tsaturation.working()\n   243\t\n   244\t\t\t\tswitch req := ptr.(type) {\n   245\t\t\t\tcase []*commitTuple:\n   246\t\t\t\t\tapplyBatch(req)\n   247\t\n   248\t\t\t\tcase *restoreFuture:\n   249\t\t\t\t\trestore(req)\n   250\t\n   251\t\t\t\tdefault:\n   252\t\t\t\t\tpanic(fmt.Errorf(\"bad type passed to fsmMutateCh: %#v\", ptr))\n   253\t\t\t\t}\n   254\t\n   255\t\t\tcase req := <-r.fsmSnapshotCh:\n   256\t\t\t\tsaturation.working()\n   257\t\n   258\t\t\t\tsnapshot(req)\n   259\t\n   260\t\t\tcase <-r.shutdownCh:\n   261\t\t\t\treturn\n   262\t\t\t}\n   263\t\t}\n   264\t}\n   265\t\n   266\t// fsmRestoreAndMeasure wraps the Restore call on an FSM to consistently measure\n   267\t// and report timing metrics. The caller is still responsible for calling Close\n   268\t// on the source in all cases.\n   269\tfunc fsmRestoreAndMeasure(logger hclog.Logger, fsm FSM, source io.ReadCloser, snapshotSize int64) error {\n   270\t\tstart := time.Now()\n   271\t\n   272\t\tcrc := newCountingReadCloser(source)\n   273\t\n   274\t\tmonitor := startSnapshotRestoreMonitor(logger, crc, snapshotSize, false)\n   275\t\tdefer monitor.StopAndWait()\n   276\t\n   277\t\tif err := fsm.Restore(crc); err != nil {\n   278\t\t\treturn err\n   279\t\t}\n   280\t\tmetrics.MeasureSince([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"restore\"}, start)\n   281\t\tmetrics.SetGauge([]string{\"raft\", \"fsm\", \"lastRestoreDuration\"},\n   282\t\t\tfloat32(time.Since(start).Milliseconds()))\n   283\t\n   284\t\treturn nil\n   285\t}\n   286\t// Copyright IBM Corp. 2013, 2025\n   287\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n   288\t\n   289\tpackage raft\n   290\t\n   291\timport (\n   292\t\t\"fmt\"\n   293\t\t\"io\"\n   294\t\t\"sync\"\n   295\t\t\"time\"\n   296\t)\n   297\t\n   298\t// Future is used to represent an action that may occur in the future.\n   299\ttype Future interface {\n   300\t\t// Error blocks until the future arrives and then returns the error status\n   301\t\t// of the future. This may be called any number of times - all calls will\n   302\t\t// return the same value, however is not OK to call this method twice\n   303\t\t// concurrently on the same Future instance.\n   304\t\t// Error will only return generic errors related to raft, such\n   305\t\t// as ErrLeadershipLost, or ErrRaftShutdown. Some operations, such as\n   306\t\t// ApplyLog, may also return errors from other methods.\n   307\t\tError() error\n   308\t}\n   309\t\n   310\t// IndexFuture is used for future actions that can result in a raft log entry\n   311\t// being created.\n   312\ttype IndexFuture interface {\n   313\t\tFuture\n   314\t\n   315\t\t// Index holds the index of the newly applied log entry.\n   316\t\t// This must not be called until after the Error method has returned.\n   317\t\tIndex() uint64\n   318\t}\n   319\t\n   320\t// ApplyFuture is used for Apply and can return the FSM response.\n   321\ttype ApplyFuture interface {\n   322\t\tIndexFuture\n   323\t\n   324\t\t// Response returns the FSM response as returned by the FSM.Apply method. This\n   325\t\t// must not be called until after the Error method has returned.\n   326\t\t// Note that if FSM.Apply returns an error, it will be returned by Response,\n   327\t\t// and not by the Error method, so it is always important to check Response\n   328\t\t// for errors from the FSM.\n   329\t\tResponse() interface{}\n   330\t}\n   331\t\n   332\t// ConfigurationFuture is used for GetConfiguration and can return the\n   333\t// latest configuration in use by Raft.\n   334\ttype ConfigurationFuture interface {\n   335\t\tIndexFuture\n   336\t\n   337\t\t// Configuration contains the latest configuration. This must\n   338\t\t// not be called until after the Error method has returned.\n   339\t\tConfiguration() Configuration\n   340\t}\n   341\t\n   342\t// SnapshotFuture is used for waiting on a user-triggered snapshot to complete.\n   343\ttype SnapshotFuture interface {\n   344\t\tFuture\n   345\t\n   346\t\t// Open is a function you can call to access the underlying snapshot and\n   347\t\t// its metadata. This must not be called until after the Error method\n   348\t\t// has returned.\n   349\t\tOpen() (*SnapshotMeta, io.ReadCloser, error)\n   350\t}\n   351\t\n   352\t// LeadershipTransferFuture is used for waiting on a user-triggered leadership\n   353\t// transfer to complete.\n   354\ttype LeadershipTransferFuture interface {\n   355\t\tFuture\n   356\t}\n   357\t\n   358\t// errorFuture is used to return a static error.\n   359\ttype errorFuture struct {\n   360\t\terr error\n   361\t}\n   362\t\n   363\tfunc (e errorFuture) Error() error {\n   364\t\treturn e.err\n   365\t}\n   366\t\n   367\tfunc (e errorFuture) Response() interface{} {\n   368\t\treturn nil\n   369\t}\n   370\t\n   371\tfunc (e errorFuture) Index() uint64 {\n   372\t\treturn 0\n   373\t}\n   374\t\n   375\t// deferError can be embedded to allow a future\n   376\t// to provide an error in the future.\n   377\ttype deferError struct {\n   378\t\terr        error\n   379\t\terrCh      chan error\n   380\t\tresponded  bool\n   381\t\tShutdownCh chan struct{}\n   382\t}\n   383\t\n   384\tfunc (d *deferError) init() {\n   385\t\td.errCh = make(chan error, 1)\n   386\t}\n   387\t\n   388\tfunc (d *deferError) Error() error {\n   389\t\tif d.err != nil {\n   390\t\t\t// Note that when we've received a nil error, this\n   391\t\t\t// won't trigger, but the channel is closed after\n   392\t\t\t// send so we'll still return nil below.\n   393\t\t\treturn d.err\n   394\t\t}\n   395\t\tif d.errCh == nil {\n   396\t\t\tpanic(\"waiting for response on nil channel\")\n   397\t\t}\n   398\t\tselect {\n   399\t\tcase d.err = <-d.errCh:\n   400\t\tcase <-d.ShutdownCh:\n   401\t\t\td.err = ErrRaftShutdown\n   402\t\t}\n   403\t\treturn d.err\n   404\t}\n   405\t\n   406\tfunc (d *deferError) respond(err error) {\n   407\t\tif d.errCh == nil {\n   408\t\t\treturn\n   409\t\t}\n   410\t\tif d.responded {\n   411\t\t\treturn\n   412\t\t}\n   413\t\td.errCh <- err\n   414\t\tclose(d.errCh)\n   415\t\td.responded = true\n   416\t}\n   417\t\n   418\t// There are several types of requests that cause a configuration entry to\n   419\t// be appended to the log. These are encoded here for leaderLoop() to process.\n   420\t// This is internal to a single server.\n   421\ttype configurationChangeFuture struct {\n   422\t\tlogFuture\n   423\t\treq configurationChangeRequest\n   424\t}\n   425\t\n   426\t// bootstrapFuture is used to attempt a live bootstrap of the cluster. See the\n   427\t// Raft object's BootstrapCluster member function for more details.\n   428\ttype bootstrapFuture struct {\n   429\t\tdeferError\n   430\t\n   431\t\t// configuration is the proposed bootstrap configuration to apply.\n   432\t\tconfiguration Configuration\n   433\t}\n   434\t\n   435\t// logFuture is used to apply a log entry and waits until\n   436\t// the log is considered committed.\n   437\ttype logFuture struct {\n   438\t\tdeferError\n   439\t\tlog      Log\n   440\t\tresponse interface{}\n   441\t\tdispatch time.Time\n   442\t}\n   443\t\n   444\tfunc (l *logFuture) Response() interface{} {\n   445\t\treturn l.response\n   446\t}\n   447\t\n   448\tfunc (l *logFuture) Index() uint64 {\n   449\t\treturn l.log.Index\n   450\t}\n   451\t\n   452\ttype shutdownFuture struct {\n   453\t\traft *Raft\n   454\t}\n   455\t\n   456\tfunc (s *shutdownFuture) Error() error {\n   457\t\tif s.raft == nil {\n   458\t\t\treturn nil\n   459\t\t}\n   460\t\ts.raft.waitShutdown()\n   461\t\tif closeable, ok := s.raft.trans.(WithClose); ok {\n   462\t\t\t_ = closeable.Close()\n   463\t\t}\n   464\t\treturn nil\n   465\t}\n   466\t\n   467\t// userSnapshotFuture is used for waiting on a user-triggered snapshot to\n   468\t// complete.\n   469\ttype userSnapshotFuture struct {\n   470\t\tdeferError\n   471\t\n   472\t\t// opener is a function used to open the snapshot. This is filled in\n   473\t\t// once the future returns with no error.\n   474\t\topener func() (*SnapshotMeta, io.ReadCloser, error)\n   475\t}\n   476\t\n   477\t// Open is a function you can call to access the underlying snapshot and its\n   478\t// metadata.\n   479\tfunc (u *userSnapshotFuture) Open() (*SnapshotMeta, io.ReadCloser, error) {\n   480\t\tif u.opener == nil {\n   481\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"no snapshot available\")\n   482\t\t}\n   483\t\t// Invalidate the opener so it can't get called multiple times,\n   484\t\t// which isn't generally safe.\n   485\t\tdefer func() {\n   486\t\t\tu.opener = nil\n   487\t\t}()\n   488\t\treturn u.opener()\n   489\t}\n   490\t\n   491\t// userRestoreFuture is used for waiting on a user-triggered restore of an\n   492\t// external snapshot to complete.\n   493\ttype userRestoreFuture struct {\n   494\t\tdeferError\n   495\t\n   496\t\t// meta is the metadata that belongs with the snapshot.\n   497\t\tmeta *SnapshotMeta\n   498\t\n   499\t\t// reader is the interface to read the snapshot contents from.\n   500\t\treader io.Reader\n   501\t}\n   502\t\n   503\t// reqSnapshotFuture is used for requesting a snapshot start.\n   504\t// It is only used internally.\n   505\ttype reqSnapshotFuture struct {\n   506\t\tdeferError\n   507\t\n   508\t\t// snapshot details provided by the FSM runner before responding\n   509\t\tindex    uint64\n   510\t\tterm     uint64\n   511\t\tsnapshot FSMSnapshot\n   512\t}\n   513\t\n   514\t// restoreFuture is used for requesting an FSM to perform a\n   515\t// snapshot restore. Used internally only.\n   516\ttype restoreFuture struct {\n   517\t\tdeferError\n   518\t\tID string\n   519\t}\n   520\t\n   521\t// verifyFuture is used to verify the current node is still\n   522\t// the leader. This is to prevent a stale read.\n   523\ttype verifyFuture struct {\n   524\t\tdeferError\n   525\t\tnotifyCh   chan *verifyFuture\n   526\t\tquorumSize int\n   527\t\tvotes      int\n   528\t\tvoteLock   sync.Mutex\n   529\t}\n   530\t\n   531\t// leadershipTransferFuture is used to track the progress of a leadership\n   532\t// transfer internally.\n   533\ttype leadershipTransferFuture struct {\n   534\t\tdeferError\n   535\t\n   536\t\tID      *ServerID\n   537\t\tAddress *ServerAddress\n   538\t}\n   539\t\n   540\t// configurationsFuture is used to retrieve the current configurations. This is\n   541\t// used to allow safe access to this information outside of the main thread.\n   542\ttype configurationsFuture struct {\n   543\t\tdeferError\n   544\t\tconfigurations configurations\n   545\t}\n   546\t\n   547\t// Configuration returns the latest configuration in use by Raft.\n   548\tfunc (c *configurationsFuture) Configuration() Configuration {\n   549\t\treturn c.configurations.latest\n   550\t}\n   551\t\n   552\t// Index returns the index of the latest configuration in use by Raft.\n   553\tfunc (c *configurationsFuture) Index() uint64 {\n   554\t\treturn c.configurations.latestIndex\n   555\t}\n   556\t\n   557\t// vote is used to respond to a verifyFuture.\n   558\t// This may block when responding on the notifyCh.\n   559\tfunc (v *verifyFuture) vote(leader bool) {\n   560\t\tv.voteLock.Lock()\n   561\t\tdefer v.voteLock.Unlock()\n   562\t\n   563\t\t// Guard against having notified already\n   564\t\tif v.notifyCh == nil {\n   565\t\t\treturn\n   566\t\t}\n   567\t\n   568\t\tif leader {\n   569\t\t\tv.votes++\n   570\t\t\tif v.votes >= v.quorumSize {\n   571\t\t\t\tv.notifyCh <- v\n   572\t\t\t\tv.notifyCh = nil\n   573\t\t\t}\n   574\t\t} else {\n   575\t\t\tv.notifyCh <- v\n   576\t\t\tv.notifyCh = nil\n   577\t\t}\n   578\t}\n   579\t\n   580\t// appendFuture is used for waiting on a pipelined append\n   581\t// entries RPC.\n   582\ttype appendFuture struct {\n   583\t\tdeferError\n   584\t\tstart time.Time\n   585\t\targs  *AppendEntriesRequest\n   586\t\tresp  *AppendEntriesResponse\n   587\t}\n   588\t\n   589\tfunc (a *appendFuture) Start() time.Time {\n   590\t\treturn a.start\n   591\t}\n   592\t\n   593\tfunc (a *appendFuture) Request() *AppendEntriesRequest {\n   594\t\treturn a.args\n   595\t}\n   596\t\n   597\tfunc (a *appendFuture) Response() *AppendEntriesResponse {\n   598\t\treturn a.resp\n   599\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source; cat -n api.go | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source; cat -n api.go | sed -n '1,240p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t// Copyright IBM Corp. 2013, 2026\n     2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n     3\t\n     4\tpackage raft\n     5\t\n     6\timport (\n     7\t\t\"errors\"\n     8\t\t\"fmt\"\n     9\t\t\"io\"\n    10\t\t\"strconv\"\n    11\t\t\"sync\"\n    12\t\t\"sync/atomic\"\n    13\t\t\"time\"\n    14\t\n    15\t\thclog \"github.com/hashicorp/go-hclog\"\n    16\t\tmetrics \"github.com/hashicorp/go-metrics\"\n    17\t)\n    18\t\n    19\tconst (\n    20\t\t// SuggestedMaxDataSize of the data in a raft log entry, in bytes.\n    21\t\t//\n    22\t\t// The value is based on current architecture, default timing, etc. Clients can\n    23\t\t// ignore this value if they want as there is no actual hard checking\n    24\t\t// within the library. As the library is enhanced this value may change\n    25\t\t// over time to reflect current suggested maximums.\n    26\t\t//\n    27\t\t// Applying log entries with data greater than this size risks RPC IO taking\n    28\t\t// too long and preventing timely heartbeat signals.  These signals are sent in serial\n    29\t\t// in current transports, potentially causing leadership instability.\n    30\t\tSuggestedMaxDataSize = 512 * 1024\n    31\t)\n    32\t\n    33\tvar (\n    34\t\t// ErrLeader is returned when an operation can't be completed on a\n    35\t\t// leader node.\n    36\t\tErrLeader = errors.New(\"node is the leader\")\n    37\t\n    38\t\t// ErrNotLeader is returned when an operation can't be completed on a\n    39\t\t// follower or candidate node.\n    40\t\tErrNotLeader = errors.New(\"node is not the leader\")\n    41\t\n    42\t\t// ErrNotVoter is returned when an operation can't be completed on a\n    43\t\t// non-voter node.\n    44\t\tErrNotVoter = errors.New(\"node is not a voter\")\n    45\t\n    46\t\t// ErrLeadershipLost is returned when a leader fails to commit a log entry\n    47\t\t// because it's been deposed in the process.\n    48\t\tErrLeadershipLost = errors.New(\"leadership lost while committing log\")\n    49\t\n    50\t\t// ErrAbortedByRestore is returned when a leader fails to commit a log\n    51\t\t// entry because it's been superseded by a user snapshot restore.\n    52\t\tErrAbortedByRestore = errors.New(\"snapshot restored while committing log\")\n    53\t\n    54\t\t// ErrRaftShutdown is returned when operations are requested against an\n    55\t\t// inactive Raft.\n    56\t\tErrRaftShutdown = errors.New(\"raft is already shutdown\")\n    57\t\n    58\t\t// ErrEnqueueTimeout is returned when a command fails due to a timeout.\n    59\t\tErrEnqueueTimeout = errors.New(\"timed out enqueuing operation\")\n    60\t\n    61\t\t// ErrNothingNewToSnapshot is returned when trying to create a snapshot\n    62\t\t// but there's nothing new committed to the FSM since we started.\n    63\t\tErrNothingNewToSnapshot = errors.New(\"nothing new to snapshot\")\n    64\t\n    65\t\t// ErrUnsupportedProtocol is returned when an operation is attempted\n    66\t\t// that's not supported by the current protocol version.\n    67\t\tErrUnsupportedProtocol = errors.New(\"operation not supported with current protocol version\")\n    68\t\n    69\t\t// ErrCantBootstrap is returned when attempt is made to bootstrap a\n    70\t\t// cluster that already has state present.\n    71\t\tErrCantBootstrap = errors.New(\"bootstrap only works on new clusters\")\n    72\t\n    73\t\t// ErrLeadershipTransferInProgress is returned when the leader is rejecting\n    74\t\t// client requests because it is attempting to transfer leadership.\n    75\t\tErrLeadershipTransferInProgress = errors.New(\"leadership transfer in progress\")\n    76\t\n    77\t\t// ErrIncompatibleLogStore is returned when the log store does not support\n    78\t\t// or implement some required methods.\n    79\t\tErrIncompatibleLogStore = errors.New(\"log store does not implement some required methods or malformed\")\n    80\t)\n    81\t\n    82\t// Raft implements a Raft node.\n    83\ttype Raft struct {\n    84\t\traftState\n    85\t\n    86\t\t// protocolVersion is used to inter-operate with Raft servers running\n    87\t\t// different versions of the library. See comments in config.go for more\n    88\t\t// details.\n    89\t\tprotocolVersion ProtocolVersion\n    90\t\n    91\t\t// applyCh is used to async send logs to the main thread to\n    92\t\t// be committed and applied to the FSM.\n    93\t\tapplyCh chan *logFuture\n    94\t\n    95\t\t// conf stores the current configuration to use. This is the most recent one\n    96\t\t// provided. All reads of config values should use the config() helper method\n    97\t\t// to read this safely.\n    98\t\tconf atomic.Value\n    99\t\n   100\t\t// confReloadMu ensures that only one thread can reload config at once since\n   101\t\t// we need to read-modify-write the atomic. It is NOT necessary to hold this\n   102\t\t// for any other operation e.g. reading config using config().\n   103\t\tconfReloadMu sync.Mutex\n   104\t\n   105\t\t// FSM is the client state machine to apply commands to\n   106\t\tfsm FSM\n   107\t\n   108\t\t// fsmMutateCh is used to send state-changing updates to the FSM. This\n   109\t\t// receives pointers to commitTuple structures when applying logs or\n   110\t\t// pointers to restoreFuture structures when restoring a snapshot. We\n   111\t\t// need control over the order of these operations when doing user\n   112\t\t// restores so that we finish applying any old log applies before we\n   113\t\t// take a user snapshot on the leader, otherwise we might restore the\n   114\t\t// snapshot and apply old logs to it that were in the pipe.\n   115\t\tfsmMutateCh chan interface{}\n   116\t\n   117\t\t// fsmSnapshotCh is used to trigger a new snapshot being taken\n   118\t\tfsmSnapshotCh chan *reqSnapshotFuture\n   119\t\n   120\t\t// lastContact is the last time we had contact from the\n   121\t\t// leader node. This can be used to gauge staleness.\n   122\t\tlastContact     time.Time\n   123\t\tlastContactLock sync.RWMutex\n   124\t\n   125\t\t// leaderAddr is the current cluster leader Address\n   126\t\tleaderAddr ServerAddress\n   127\t\t// LeaderID is the current cluster leader ID\n   128\t\tleaderID   ServerID\n   129\t\tleaderLock sync.RWMutex\n   130\t\n   131\t\t// leaderCh is used to notify of leadership changes\n   132\t\tleaderCh chan bool\n   133\t\n   134\t\t// leaderState used only while state is leader\n   135\t\tleaderState leaderState\n   136\t\n   137\t\t// candidateFromLeadershipTransfer is used to indicate that this server became\n   138\t\t// candidate because the leader tries to transfer leadership. This flag is\n   139\t\t// used in RequestVoteRequest to express that a leadership transfer is going\n   140\t\t// on.\n   141\t\tcandidateFromLeadershipTransfer atomic.Bool\n   142\t\n   143\t\t// Stores our local server ID, used to avoid sending RPCs to ourself\n   144\t\tlocalID ServerID\n   145\t\n   146\t\t// Stores our local addr\n   147\t\tlocalAddr ServerAddress\n   148\t\n   149\t\t// Used for our logging\n   150\t\tlogger hclog.Logger\n   151\t\n   152\t\t// LogStore provides durable storage for logs\n   153\t\tlogs LogStore\n   154\t\n   155\t\t// Used to request the leader to make configuration changes.\n   156\t\tconfigurationChangeCh chan *configurationChangeFuture\n   157\t\n   158\t\t// Tracks the latest configuration and latest committed configuration from\n   159\t\t// the log/snapshot.\n   160\t\tconfigurations configurations\n   161\t\n   162\t\t// Holds a copy of the latest configuration which can be read independently\n   163\t\t// of the main loop.\n   164\t\tlatestConfiguration atomic.Value\n   165\t\n   166\t\t// RPC chan comes from the transport layer\n   167\t\trpcCh <-chan RPC\n   168\t\n   169\t\t// Shutdown channel to exit, protected to prevent concurrent exits\n   170\t\tshutdown     bool\n   171\t\tshutdownCh   chan struct{}\n   172\t\tshutdownLock sync.Mutex\n   173\t\n   174\t\t// snapshots is used to store and retrieve snapshots\n   175\t\tsnapshots SnapshotStore\n   176\t\n   177\t\t// userSnapshotCh is used for user-triggered snapshots\n   178\t\tuserSnapshotCh chan *userSnapshotFuture\n   179\t\n   180\t\t// userRestoreCh is used for user-triggered restores of external\n   181\t\t// snapshots\n   182\t\tuserRestoreCh chan *userRestoreFuture\n   183\t\n   184\t\t// stable is a StableStore implementation for durable state\n   185\t\t// It provides stable storage for many fields in raftState\n   186\t\tstable StableStore\n   187\t\n   188\t\t// The transport layer we use\n   189\t\ttrans Transport\n   190\t\n   191\t\t// verifyCh is used to async send verify futures to the main thread\n   192\t\t// to verify we are still the leader\n   193\t\tverifyCh chan *verifyFuture\n   194\t\n   195\t\t// configurationsCh is used to get the configuration data safely from\n   196\t\t// outside of the main thread.\n   197\t\tconfigurationsCh chan *configurationsFuture\n   198\t\n   199\t\t// bootstrapCh is used to attempt an initial bootstrap from outside of\n   200\t\t// the main thread.\n   201\t\tbootstrapCh chan *bootstrapFuture\n   202\t\n   203\t\t// List of observers and the mutex that protects them. The observers list\n   204\t\t// is indexed by an artificial ID which is used for deregistration.\n   205\t\tobserversLock sync.RWMutex\n   206\t\tobservers     map[uint64]*Observer\n   207\t\n   208\t\t// leadershipTransferCh is used to start a leadership transfer from outside of\n   209\t\t// the main thread.\n   210\t\tleadershipTransferCh chan *leadershipTransferFuture\n   211\t\n   212\t\t// leaderNotifyCh is used to tell leader that config has changed\n   213\t\tleaderNotifyCh chan struct{}\n   214\t\n   215\t\t// followerNotifyCh is used to tell followers that config has changed\n   216\t\tfollowerNotifyCh chan struct{}\n   217\t\n   218\t\t// mainThreadSaturation measures the saturation of the main raft goroutine.\n   219\t\tmainThreadSaturation *saturationMetric\n   220\t\n   221\t\t// preVoteDisabled control if the pre-vote feature is activated,\n   222\t\t// prevote feature is disabled if set to true.\n   223\t\tpreVoteDisabled bool\n   224\t\n   225\t\t// noLegacyTelemetry allows to skip the legacy metrics to avoid duplicates.\n   226\t\t// legacy metrics are those that have `_peer_name` as metric suffix instead as labels.\n   227\t\t// e.g: raft_replication_heartbeat_peer0\n   228\t\tnoLegacyTelemetry bool\n   229\t\n   230\t\t// RestoreCommittedLogs is used to enable restore committed logs mode\n   231\t\t// restore committed logs mode is disabled if set to false.\n   232\t\tRestoreCommittedLogs bool\n   233\t}\n   234\t\n   235\t// BootstrapCluster initializes a server's storage with the given cluster\n   236\t// configuration. This should only be called at the beginning of time for the\n   237\t// cluster with an identical configuration listing all Voter servers. There is\n   238\t// no need to bootstrap Nonvoter and Staging servers.\n   239\t//\n   240\t// A cluster can only be bootstrapped once from a single participating Voter\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
