loss (servers_after=1), separating the scanning bound from generic restart damage.\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"active\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"gaps\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@restart_config\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"When a snapshot exists but the newest configuration entry was committed after that snapshot (ConfigurationIndex older than the entry), does the same skipped committed prefix make the restarted node adopt the older configuration, permanently losing the newer membership (and its quorum size), and does that stale configuration later justify a different decision or duty completion?\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"experiment\\\": {\n    \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@restart_config\\\",\n    \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n    \\\"files\\\": {\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\": \\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\"},\n    \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"newraft_scan\\\", \\\"restore_committed\\\", \\\"follower_abort\\\"],\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"In-process single-voter Cluster: bootstrap a configuration entry, become leader, apply five commands, then restart the node on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore with a fresh transport. Three cases: restore_committed_logs on with no snapshot; off with no snapshot; on with a snapshot taken before the restart. Observations are the node's configuration size (GetConfiguration), whether it reaches Leader again, applied/commit indices, and staged commit index at restart.\\\",\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n        \\\"RestoreCommittedLogs is a documented public Config field (config.go 243-254) that is enabled by the application; the probe only supplies that documented configuration.\\\",\n        \\\"The existing test TestRaft_RestoreCommittedLogs always snapshots before restarting (raft_test.go 1183-1280), so the configuration-in-log path is not covered by it.\\\",\n        \\\"No snapshot is taken in the no-snapshot cases (SnapshotThreshold huge, SnapshotInterval 10m), which is normal operation for clusters below the snapshot threshold.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"excluded\\\": [\n        \\\"Multi-node clusters and network partitions: the probe is a single-voter cluster, so the observed election abort is a progress loss and the vote-check consequence is source-read, not executed here.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"parameters\\\": {\\\"protocol_version\\\": 3, \\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\": 50, \\\"election_timeout_ms\\\": 50, \\\"trailing_logs\\\": 10}\n    },\n    \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"Fresh in-memory transport, InmemCommitTrackingStore log store, InmemStore stable store, InmemSnapshotStore; BootstrapCluster writes the single-voter configuration at index 1/term 1; first NewRaft elects the node as leader; five Apply commands are committed; optional user snapshot; Shutdown; second NewRaft on the same stores with a new transport sharing the same address. The harness never fabricates log entries or configuration state: all durable state comes from real bootstrap, real elections, real commits and a real snapshot.\\\",\n    \\\"comparisons\\\": [\n      {\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"post_restart\\\",\n        \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"mode\\\"],\n        \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"restore_on_no_snapshot\\\",\n        \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"servers_after\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1},\n        \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"mode\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"restore_on_no_snapshot\\\"},\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"snapshot_count\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 0}\n        ],\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"With RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and no snapshot, the restarted node must still report the bootstrapped voter.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"post_restart\\\",\n        \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"mode\\\"],\n        \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"restore_off_no_snapshot\\\",\n        \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"servers_after\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1},\n        \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"mode\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"restore_off_no_snapshot\\\"},\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"snapshot_count\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 0}\n        ],\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Control: the same restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps the configuration, isolating the committed-prefix replay as the cause.\\\"\n      },\n      {\n        \\\"event\\\": \\\"post_restart\\\",\n        \\\"identity_fields\\\": [\\\"mode\\\"],\n        \\\"admission_alias\\\": \\\"restore_on_with_snapshot\\\",\n        \\\"assertion\\\": {\\\"field\\\": \\\"servers_after\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1},\n        \\\"applicability_conditions\\\": [\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"mode\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"restore_on_with_snapshot\\\"},\n          {\\\"field\\\": \\\"snapshot_count\\\", \\\"op\\\": \\\"eq\\\", \\\"value\\\": 1}\n        ],\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"Control: with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and a snapshot that carries the configuration, the restarted node keeps the configuration, showing that the loss is specific to configurations that only exist in the skipped committed log prefix.\\\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@restart_config\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"newraft_scan\\\", \\\"restore_committed\\\", \\\"newraft_doc\\\", \\\"cfg_doc\\\", \\\"snapshot_config\\\", \\\"process_config_entry\\\", \\\"follower_abort\\\", \\\"vote_config_checks\\\", \\\"prevote_config_checks\\\"],\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"violated\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"asserted\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"NewRaft documents that existing state such as logs and peers is restored (api.go 504-507) and RestoreCommittedLogs is documented only as replaying committed logs before startup (config.go 243-254); nothing waives configuration recovery. The code nevertheless bounds the configuration scan by max(lastSnapshot, lastApplied)+1 (api.go 611-613) while restoreFromCommittedLogs has already raised lastApplied to the persisted commit index (api.go 723-755). processConfigurationLogEntry is the only path that turns a log entry into r.configurations (raft.go 1605-1623), so configuration entries inside the committed prefix are dropped whenever a snapshot does not carry them (snapshot path: api.go 645-689). Consequence: after a plain restart of a bootstrapped node with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled and no snapshot, r.configurations.latest is empty, so runFollower refuses to campaign ('no known peers', raft.go 230-234) and both requestVote and requestPreVote skip their membership checks because they are gated on a non-empty Servers list (raft.go 1663-1672, 1780-1784). The rule that decides the decision is therefore evaluated against an empty configuration rather than the replicated one.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The existing TestRaft_RestoreCommittedLogs (raft_test.go 1183-1280) passes: it always snapshots before restarting, so its configuration comes from snapshot metadata rather than from the log, and the same probe shows that a snapshot-carried configuration masks the loss.\\\",\n        \\\"The loss is not caused by the commit-tracking store or by replaying logs to the FSM per se: the control restart with RestoreCommittedLogs=false on identical stores and log contents keeps the configuration and wins the election again.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The executed probe is a single-voter in-memory cluster; the multi-node consequences (a node that grants votes to servers it cannot be shown to contain, or a node whose quorum size is computed from a stale configuration) are read from source, not executed.\\\",\n        \\\"The persisted commit index used at restart is what the store reported (6 while the log ended at 7); the drop of the configuration entry does not depend on that lag, but the exact boundary of what is skipped does.\\\",\n        \\\"Whether upstream intends applications to always snapshot before enabling this option is not stated anywhere in the captured sources; the Config documentation mentions no such requirement.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission draft/update.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"af7ab1df563f4f5686eb47935464cf57\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2.633565451000095, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"submission\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Submission file is missing or escapes the draft directory\", \"allowed\": []}], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
